00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Their streets. Their rules.

2
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Brick Mansions is a action, crime, drama film directed by Camille Delamarre.

3
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
In a dystopian Detroit, grand houses that once housed the wealthy
are now homes of the city's most-dangerous criminals.

4
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Surrounding the area is a giant wall to keep the rest of Detroit safe.

5
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
For undercover cop Damien Collier, every day is a battle against corruption as
he struggles to bring his father's killer, Tremaine, to justice.

6
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Meanwhile, Damien and an ex-con named Lino work together to
save the city from a plot to destroy it.

7
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Damien Collier, played by Paul Walker.

8
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Lino, played by David Belle.

9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Tremaine, played by RZA.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Yeti, played by Robert Maillet.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
George the Greek, played by Carlo Rota.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Mayor's Assistant, played by Kalinka Pétrie.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Brick Mansions is a 2014 action film starring Paul Walker, David
Belle, RZA, Goûchy Boy, Catalina Denis and Carlo Rota.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film was directed by Camille Delamarre and written by Luc
Besson, Robert Mark Kamen and Bibi Naceri.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
A co-production between France, Canada and the United States, it is a remake of
the 2004 French film District 13, in which Belle had also starred.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
This movie was released on April 25, 2014, five months after Walker's
death on November 30, 2013, and is dedicated to him.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
This was Walker's last fully completed film before his death and his
penultimate film, followed by his final film appearance in Furious 7.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, atomic
bomb, gangster, dystopia, ghetto.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The tone is emotional.
